<body>
    <h1>Password and User Types in IGEL OS 12</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <p>
<style>[data-colorid=3Dw4jtob93t3]{color:#202124} html[data-color-mode=3Dda=
rk] [data-colorid=3Dw4jtob93t3]{color:#dbdcdf}[data-colorid=3Dg1g8lnjw4q]{c=
olor:#333333} html[data-color-mode=3Ddark] [data-colorid=3Dg1g8lnjw4q]{colo=
r:#cccccc}[data-colorid=3Dacrqflc09w]{color:#202124} html[data-color-mode=
=3Ddark] [data-colorid=3Dacrqflc09w]{color:#dbdcdf}</style>The following ar=
ticle provides details on the user types and their roles in IGEL OS. You ca=
n configure passwords for the user types to protect your endpoint devices a=
gainst unwanted changes.&nbsp;</p>
<hr>
<p>Menu path:&nbsp; <strong>Security &gt; Password</strong></p>
<p></p><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-left-wrapper c=
onfluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image ima=
ge-left" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"c1750de16242e40c1a3827521748=
808d8836d53e1d99a156477f39adc86d41dd" data-image-src=3D"https://igel-jira.a=
tlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/73302358/OS12_Password.png?version=
=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1716364680071&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2=
" data-height=3D"912" data-width=3D"1126" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"=
0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73309347" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" =
data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=
=3D"OS12_Password.png" data-base-url=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wik=
i" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-con=
tainer-id=3D"73302358" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"7" data-me=
dia-id=3D"46093ab1-0f92-4f3b-94e9-3b18bd707856" data-media-type=3D"file" he=
ight=3D"378"></span>
<h2 id=3D"PasswordandUserTypesinIGELOS12-IGELSetupPasswordProtection">IGEL =
Setup Password Protection</h2>
<p>Configure the administrator password to create the password protection f=
or the<strong> </strong>IGEL Setup. You can also configure the setup admini=
strator and the setup user to allow additional access to the IGEL Setup. Fo=
r more information, see <a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spa=
ces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302858/Setup" data-linked-resource-id=3D"7330285=
8" data-linked-resource-version=3D"4" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Se=
tup</a> .</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p><span data-colorid=3D"g1g8lnjw4q">The assignment of the administrator pa=
ssword is a prerequisite for all other rights assignments. Even if the admi=
nistrator wants to leave the administration of the IGEL Setup to the setup =
administrator, the administrator password must be set.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>If you do not configure any password, the IGEL Setup can be opened witho=
ut password protection.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"PasswordandUserTypesinIGELOS12-UserRights">User Rights</h2>
<p>The user types have the following access rights:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Administrator</strong>: If configured, the administrator passwor=
d protects the following critical actions/areas from unauthorized access:</=
p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>IGEL Setup</p></li>
<li>
<p>Reset to factory defaults boot mode.&nbsp;(For more information, see <a =
href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73=
302494/Boot+Menu+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302494" data-l=
inked-resource-version=3D"6" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Boot Menu i=
n IGEL OS 12</a> .)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Accessing the local terminal as <code>root</code>. (For more information=
, see <a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE=
/pages/73302207/Terminals+in+IGEL+OS" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302207" =
data-linked-resource-version=3D"5" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Termi=
nals in IGEL OS</a> .)</p></li>
<li>
<p>Virtual console access. (For more information, see <a href=3D"https://ig=
el-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302715/Access+Cont=
rol+to+the+Display+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302715" data=
-linked-resource-version=3D"3" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Access Co=
ntrol to the Display in IGEL OS 12</a> .)</p></li>
<li>
<p>sessions, for which <strong>Administrator</strong> is set under <strong>=
Password protection</strong>. (For more information, see <a href=3D"https:/=
/igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302709/Starting=
+Methods+for+Apps" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302709" data-linked-resourc=
e-version=3D"5" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Starting Methods for App=
s</a> .)<br><br>
If configured, the administrator can access the following with a password:<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p>Unlocking the screenlock. (For more information, see&nbsp;<a href=3D"htt=
ps://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302255/Scre=
enlock+Screensaver+Options+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"733022=
55" data-linked-resource-version=3D"8" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">S=
creenloock/Screensaver Options in IGEL OS 12</a> .)</p></li>
<li>
<p><span data-colorid=3D"w4jtob93t3">Secure Shell</span> <span class=3D"leg=
acy-color-text-blue3"> &nbsp;(SSH)</span>. (For more information, see <a hr=
ef=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/7330=
2060/SSH+Access+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302060" data-li=
nked-resource-version=3D"4" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">SSH Access i=
n IGEL OS 12</a> .)<br><br></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong> <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"be24361c-6942=
-4a27-810b-b39ca16dad56">Setup administrator</span> </strong> <span class=
=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"be24361c-6942-4a27-810b-b39ca16dad56=
">:</span> If configured, the setup administrator can access the following =
with a password:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>IGEL Setup<br><br></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong> <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"42146649-9b67=
-429a-aa55-086e98527b8d">Setup user</span> </strong> : If configured, the s=
etup user can access the following with a password:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"94a38b4f-0571-4cca-b2a=
e-7c0e4efcb2a8">IGEL Setup. (</span><span class=3D"legacy-color-text-blue3"=
><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"94a38b4f-0571-4cca-b2ae-=
7c0e4efcb2a8">Unlike in OS 11, in OS 12 the Setup User can access all parts=
 of Setup.)</span></span></p></li>
<li>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"cc66f2ed-87ae-497c-ac1=
b-424199b6e299">sessions, for which </span><strong><span class=3D"inline-co=
mment-marker" data-ref=3D"cc66f2ed-87ae-497c-ac1b-424199b6e299">Setup user<=
/span></strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"cc66f2ed-8=
7ae-497c-ac1b-424199b6e299"> is set under </span><strong><span class=3D"inl=
ine-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"cc66f2ed-87ae-497c-ac1b-424199b6e299">Passw=
ord protection</span></strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-re=
f=3D"cc66f2ed-87ae-497c-ac1b-424199b6e299">. (For</span> more information, =
see <a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/p=
ages/73302709/Starting+Methods+for+Apps" data-linked-resource-id=3D"7330270=
9" data-linked-resource-version=3D"5" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">St=
arting Methods for Apps</a> .)</p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-war=
ning">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-error confluence-inform=
ation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>If you configure a Setup user in OS 12, they have effectively the same S=
etup permissions as the Administrator. This includes running Custom Command=
s (command execution with privilege escalation).</p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p></li>
</ul></li>
<li>
<p><strong>User</strong> : If configured, the user can access the following=
 with a password:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>the&nbsp;terminal session as <code>user</code>. (For more information, s=
ee <a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pa=
ges/73302207/Terminals+in+IGEL+OS" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302207" dat=
a-linked-resource-version=3D"5" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Terminal=
s in IGEL OS</a> .)</p></li>
<li>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"dc9c200b-2768-4778-8ef=
2-23a5bbdc032c">sessions, for which </span><strong><span class=3D"inline-co=
mment-marker" data-ref=3D"dc9c200b-2768-4778-8ef2-23a5bbdc032c">User</span>=
</strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"dc9c200b-2768-47=
78-8ef2-23a5bbdc032c"> is set under </span><strong><span class=3D"inline-co=
mment-marker" data-ref=3D"dc9c200b-2768-4778-8ef2-23a5bbdc032c">Password pr=
otection</span></strong><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"d=
c9c200b-2768-4778-8ef2-23a5bbdc032c">. (For more information, see </span><a=
 href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/7=
3302709/Starting+Methods+for+Apps" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302709" dat=
a-linked-resource-version=3D"5" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Starting=
 Methods for Apps</a> <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"dc9=
c200b-2768-4778-8ef2-23a5bbdc032c">.)</span></p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-inf=
ormation">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-informa=
tion-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<p>You can also use the&nbsp; <strong>User</strong> password for starting t=
he screenlock:&nbsp; <strong>User Interface &gt; Screenlock / Screensaver &=
gt;</strong> &nbsp; <strong>Starting Methods for Session &gt; Password prot=
ection</strong>. For details, see <a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.ne=
t/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302271/Screenlock+Screensaver+in+IGEL+=
OS+12" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302271" data-linked-resource-version=3D=
"4" data-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Screenlock / Screensaver in IGEL OS =
12</a> .</p>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"68a358e6-df7d-4d29-92b=
b-fa9dacaa5235">However, note</span> the following: &nbsp;</p>
<p>The&nbsp; <strong>User</strong> &nbsp;is not the same as the local user =
configured under&nbsp;<strong>Security &gt; Logon &gt; Local User</strong>.=
 For unlocking the screenlock, the local user password (not the user passwo=
rd) is used. For details, see&nbsp;<a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.n=
et/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302193/Local+User+Login+in+IGEL+OS+12=
" data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302193" data-linked-resource-version=3D"4" d=
ata-linked-resource-type=3D"page">Local User Login in IGEL OS 12</a> and <a=
 href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/7=
3302255/Screenlock+Screensaver+Options+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-linked-resource-=
id=3D"73302255" data-linked-resource-version=3D"8" data-linked-resource-typ=
e=3D"page">Screenloock/Screensaver Options in IGEL OS 12</a> .<br></p>
</div>
</div>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>User account for remote access</strong>: If configured, the <cod=
e>ruser</code> can access the device via <span data-colorid=3D"acrqflc09w">=
Secure Shell</span> <span class=3D"legacy-color-text-blue3"> &nbsp;(SSH)</s=
pan>. (For more information, see <a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlassian.net=
/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302060/SSH+Access+in+IGEL+OS+12" data-l=
inked-resource-id=3D"73302060" data-linked-resource-version=3D"4" data-link=
ed-resource-type=3D"page">SSH Access in IGEL OS 12</a> .)</p></li>
</ul>
<p></p>
<h2 id=3D"PasswordandUserTypesinIGELOS12-Administrator">Administrator</h2>
<p><strong>Use password</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 Administrator password protection is enabled and further user =
types can be configured. The password is set by clicking&nbsp; <strong>Set =
password</strong>.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 &nbsp;Administrator access is granted without password protect=
ion. No password can be configured for the user (<code>user</code>), the se=
tup user, and the setup administrator. (Default)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Change password</strong></p>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"af465eba-c1ff-4f5f-91f=
2-7f9f0bab9ca9">Click the button to set a new</span> password.</p>
<p></p>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-not=
e">
<span class=3D"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-warning confluence-info=
rmation-macro-icon"></span>
<div class=3D"confluence-information-macro-body">
<h3 id=3D"PasswordandUserTypesinIGELOS12-Effectsonlocalterminalaccess">Effe=
cts on local terminal access</h3>
<p>Setting an administrator password has the following effects on the acces=
s to local terminals:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>For logging in as&nbsp; <code>root</code>, the administrator password mu=
st be entered.</p></li>
<li>
<p>Logging in as&nbsp; <code>user</code> &nbsp;is no longer possible by def=
ault. However, you can allow access for&nbsp; <code>user</code> &nbsp; by m=
aking the following settings:</p></li>
<li>
<p></p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>Enable the registry key&nbsp; <code>system.security.usershell</code> &nb=
sp;(Default: Disabled).</p></li>
<li>
<p>Set a user password.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<p>For logging in as&nbsp; <code>user</code>, the user password will have t=
o be entered.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"PasswordandUserTypesinIGELOS12-SetupAdministrator">Setup Administ=
rator</h2>
<p><strong>Setup administrator access</strong></p>
<p>This option is only available if an administrator password is set.</p>
<p>=E2=98=91 The setup administrator can access the IGEL Setup with a passw=
ord. The password is set by clicking&nbsp; <strong>Set password</strong>.</=
p>
<p>=E2=98=90 The setup administrator cannot access the IGEL Setup. (Default=
)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Change password</strong></p>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"be36d6ef-1087-4754-a62=
1-557046764292">Click the button to set a ne</span>w password.</p>
<h2 id=3D"PasswordandUserTypesinIGELOS12-SetupUser">Setup User</h2>
<p><strong>Setup user access</strong></p>
<p>This option is only available if an administrator password is set.</p>
<p>=E2=98=91 Setup user password protection is enabled. The password is set=
 by clicking&nbsp; <strong>Set password</strong>.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 The setup user cannot access the IGEL Setup. Sessions, for whi=
ch <strong>Setup user</strong> is set under <strong>Password protection</st=
rong> will not have password protection. (Default)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Change password</strong></p>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"e6a23ce0-b122-46c8-a0b=
d-539332fdaee0">Click the button to set</span> a new password.</p>
<h2 id=3D"PasswordandUserTypesinIGELOS12-User">User</h2>
<p><strong>Use password</strong></p>
<p>This option is only available if an administrator password is set.</p>
<p>=E2=98=91 User password protection is enabled. The password is set by cl=
icking&nbsp; <strong>Set password</strong>.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 If an administrator password is set, the user (<code>user</cod=
e>) cannot log in to the device via the local terminal. Sessions, for which=
 <strong>User</strong> is set under <strong>Password protection</strong> wi=
ll not have password protection. (Default)</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Change password</strong></p>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"2308edba-1aaa-4db5-993=
a-50c9fa372b03">Click the button to set</span> a new password.</p>
<h2 id=3D"PasswordandUserTypesinIGELOS12-UserAccountforRemoteAccess">User A=
ccount for Remote Access</h2>
<p><strong>Enable login</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 The remote user (<code>ruser</code>) can log in to the device =
via SSH.&nbsp;(Default)</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 Logging in via SSH is not possible.</p>
<p>For further SSH access settings, see <a href=3D"https://igel-jira.atlass=
ian.net/wiki/spaces/IGELOS12BSDOCE/pages/73302060/SSH+Access+in+IGEL+OS+12"=
 data-linked-resource-id=3D"73302060" data-linked-resource-version=3D"4" da=
ta-linked-resource-type=3D"page">SSH Access in IGEL OS 12</a> .</p>
<p></p>
<p><strong>Use password</strong></p>
<p>=E2=98=91 A password is needed to log in via SSH. The password is set by=
 clicking&nbsp; <strong>Set password</strong>.</p>
<p>=E2=98=90 No password is needed to log in via SSH. (Default)</p>
<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>
<p><strong>Change password</strong></p>
<p><span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"64cf7127-ebdc-4bee-9ef=
c-77d67efd59fa">Click the button to set</span> a new password.</p>
<p></p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
